{"_id":"wmPlayerGuide001","name":"Wrathmaker — Player Guide","ownership":{"default":2},"pages":[{"_id":"wmGuidePage00001","name":"Welcome & quick reference","type":"text","sort":100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Welcome &amp; quick reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Your central reference for Wrathmaker's additions to Pathfinder 2e. Use the journal's page list to jump to a topic. These are campaign house rules, not replacements for every PF2e rule.</p><p>The tables show the module's current defaults. Your character sheet, item and Workbench show your campaign's configured values; ask the GM if they differ. Optional features may not be enabled.</p><ul><li>Choose a profession on your character sheet; its feats appear under Profession Feats.</li><li>Track Hero Points on your character and Nephilim Points on the party.</li><li>Use the party Exploration tab for travel and the Workbench for crafting, gathering and disassembly.</li><li>Look under Pathfinder 2E Wrathmaker in Compendium Packs for the additional items, professions and guides.</li></ul><p>The Mark pages at the end include sources and descriptions. A listed Mark is a reference, not an automatic grant: your item and artisan must qualify.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00002","name":"Professions & specialisations","type":"text","sort":200000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Professions &amp; specialisations</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Choose one starting profession at level 1. It grants its named Lore, Additional Lore, Specialty Crafting and its determined bonus feat. Profession Feats are grouped beneath their parent profession.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Profession</th><th>Additional feat</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blacksmithing</td><td>Quick Repair</td></tr><tr><td>Alchemy</td><td>Alchemical Crafting</td></tr><tr><td>Enchanting</td><td>Magical Crafting</td></tr><tr><td>Leatherwork</td><td>Experienced Tracker</td></tr><tr><td>Carpentry</td><td>Hefty Hauler</td></tr><tr><td>Stonemasonry</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Glassmaking</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Pottery</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Weaving</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Bookmaking</td><td>To be determined</td></tr><tr><td>Tailoring</td><td>To be determined</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Lore proficiency is trained at level 1, expert at 3, master at 7 and legendary at 15. At levels 4, 10 and 16, choose a specialty of your starting profession or learn a new profession. Specialty Lore follows the same proficiency progression.</p><p>Relevant profession checks receive a +2 circumstance bonus. This does not stack with another circumstance bonus such as Specialty Crafting on the same check. Each specialisation has Signature, Mastery and Legacy sections; use its current description, and do not treat unresolved placeholders as granted benefits.</p><h2>Blacksmithing</h2><ul><li><strong>Hellforging</strong>: Infernal weapons and armour shaped through fear, flame, sacrifice, and battle-tested tempers.</li><li><strong>Radiant Forging</strong>: Protective and cleansing equipment that channels light, healing, and defence of others.</li><li><strong>Azlanti Artifice</strong>: Ancient magitek, reverse-engineered machinery, original devices, and advanced infrastructure.</li></ul><h2>Alchemy</h2><ul><li><strong>Grand Apothecary</strong>: Refined potions and elixirs tailored for stability, duration, delivery, or specialised outcomes.</li><li><strong>Venomcraft</strong>: Custom toxins shaped around delivery, persistence, concealment, onset, or a chosen quarry.</li><li><strong>Transmutative Alchemy</strong>: Controlled material conversion and the creation of specialist composite substances.</li></ul><h2>Enchanting</h2><ul><li><strong>Aethercasting</strong>: Controlled magical enhancements and the incremental upgrading of empowered items.</li><li><strong>Essencebinding</strong>: Approved item traits and harvested essences bound safely into qualifying equipment.</li><li><strong>Runecarving</strong>: Efficient rune creation, upgrading, transfer, and linked Rune Echoes.</li></ul><h2>Leatherwork</h2><ul><li><strong>Wyrmcraft</strong>: Dragon-scale equipment that preserves an adaptation belonging to the source dragon.</li><li><strong>Beastbinding</strong>: Prepared hides that preserve a useful natural quality of the creature they came from.</li><li><strong>Mantlecraft</strong>: Prestigious and protective mantles, cloaks, robes, and environmental garments.</li></ul><h2>Carpentry</h2><ul><li><strong>Warbowyer</strong>: Engineered bows, crossbows, ballistae, loading systems, and specialist ammunition.</li><li><strong>Masterwright</strong>: Bridges, roads, docks, fieldworks, buildings, and major wooden structures.</li><li><strong>Warcarving</strong>: Combat forms and utility carvings applied to wooden weapons, shields, and tools.</li></ul><h2>Stonemasonry</h2><ul><li><strong>Megalithics</strong>: Monumental works, fortresses, roads, aqueducts, walls, and major civil structures.</li><li><strong>Runemasonry</strong>: Wardstones and enduring magical inscriptions that protect places rather than carried items.</li><li><strong>Titanmasonry</strong>: Stone wargear, constructs, siege engines, and powerful Titanic forms.</li></ul><h2>Glassmaking</h2><ul><li><strong>Prismcraft</strong>: Lenses and prisms that focus, split, redirect, or transform light and magical energy.</li><li><strong>Mirrorcraft</strong>: Reflective magic, illusions, scrying, communication, and linked mirrors.</li><li><strong>Aetherglass</strong>: Mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry, construct cores, and powered components.</li></ul><h2>Pottery</h2><ul><li><strong>Ceramancy</strong>: Living clay, terracotta constructs, ceramic armour, figurines, and guardians.</li><li><strong>Reliquarycraft</strong>: Vessels that preserve blessings, curses, spirits, essences, and planar energy.</li><li><strong>Pyroceramics</strong>: Crucibles, bomb casings, heat-resistant vessels, magical kilns, and industrial ceramics.</li></ul><h2>Weaving</h2><ul><li><strong>Aetherweaving</strong>: Manathread and magical cloth that carry enchantments, wards, and arcane patterns.</li><li><strong>Ironweaving</strong>: Warcloth, armour backing, nets, ropes, bowstrings, sails, and resilient reinforcement.</li><li><strong>Heraldweaving</strong>: Standards, banners, and tapestries supporting morale, identity, armies, and prestige.</li></ul><h2>Bookmaking</h2><ul><li><strong>Grimoirecraft</strong>: Living spellbooks and codices with enhanced memory, resonance, organisation, and access.</li><li><strong>Chroniclecraft</strong>: Lore, formulae, techniques, and Codices of Mastery that make recorded knowledge usable.</li><li><strong>Grand Cartography</strong>: Master atlases for exploration, resources, roads, armies, settlements, and expansion.</li></ul><h2>Tailoring</h2><ul><li><strong>Battlestitching</strong>: Combat garments and armour liners designed for movement, access, protection, and adaptation.</li><li><strong>Veilcraft</strong>: Supernatural disguises, stealth clothing, concealing mantles, and perception-altering garments.</li><li><strong>Regaliacraft</strong>: Vestments of authority supporting diplomacy, leadership, morale, royal courts, and prestige.</li></ul></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00003","name":"Hero & Nephilim Points","type":"text","sort":300000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Hero &amp; Nephilim Points</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><h2>Hero Points</h2><p>You can hold up to 10 Hero Points. Unspent points carry over between sessions. Use the normal character-sheet control; ordinary Hero Point spending rules still apply unless your GM says otherwise.</p><h2>Nephilim Points</h2><p>The party has a separate shared tracker from 0 to 10 in its header. These points persist with the party. Wrathmaker tracks the total but does not define automatic powers or spending benefits; your GM explains when they are earned or spent.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00004","name":"Equipment, Core materials & Apex items","type":"text","sort":400000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Equipment, Core materials &amp; Apex items</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>A crafted item combines a PF2e base item, a Core material and optional Artisan Marks. Core progression replaces rune-style progression on that item; do not add the replaced rune benefits a second time.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Weapon attack</th><th>Extra damage dice</th><th>Spell attack / DC</th><th>Armor AC / saves</th><th>Capacity</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>+0</td><td>0</td><td>+0</td><td>+0 / +0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>+1</td><td>1</td><td>+1</td><td>+1 / +1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>+2</td><td>2</td><td>+2</td><td>+2 / +2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>+3</td><td>2</td><td>+3</td><td>+3 / +3</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>+4</td><td>3</td><td>+4</td><td>+4 / +4</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>+5</td><td>4</td><td>+5</td><td>+5 / +5</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Weapon dice are additional dice, not flat damage. Shields gain +3 Hardness and +30 HP per Core progression step. The displayed item includes applicable modifications.</p><h2>Spell Focus</h2><p>A held Metal or Wood focus grants its Core spellcasting bonus to spell attacks and DCs, not spell damage, slots or proficiency. Only the strongest held focus applies.</p><h2>Dragon Scales</h2><p>Scales enhance Metal or Leather/Hide armor. Hatchling, Juvenile, Youth, Adult, Ancient and Arch Dragon grant default resistance values 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20. Black grants acid, Blue electricity, Green poison, Red fire and White cold resistance while the armor is equipped.</p><h2>Apex ability equipment</h2><p>Wrathmaker's 30 worn items grant +1 to +5 to Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma. Wear and invest the item, then use its circled A on the character sheet. Different attributes can be active together; for the same attribute only the strongest applies. Belts, rings, amulets, circlets, sashes and brooches form the collection. These are campaign rewards, not a priced shop list.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00005","name":"Resource catalogue","type":"text","sort":500000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Resource catalogue</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Resources are Equipment with the Precious tag. Each inventory unit is one Resource Unit, including named lots of crystals or scales. Five units weigh 1 Bulk; ten weigh 2 Bulk. Prices below are full unit values, before a sale discount. Existing older inventory copies may still appear as Treasure.</p><p>Tier levels are 1, 4, 8, 12, 16 and 20, with default level-based DCs 15, 19, 24, 30, 35 and 40. The actual attempt may have an adjustment.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>Tier</th><th>Level</th><th>Unit value</th><th>Unit Bulk</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Iron Ingot</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Steel Ingot</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Cold Iron Ingot</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Mithril Ingot</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adamantium Ingot</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Dark Iron Ingot</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Softwood Lumber</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hardwood Lumber</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Blackwood Lumber</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Darkmoon Lumber</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Starwood Lumber</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Godwood Lumber</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Fieldstone Block</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Granite Block</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Obsidian Block</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Runestone Block</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Celestite Block</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Worldstone Block</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Rawhide Sheet</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hardened Leather Sheet</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ironhide Sheet</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Moonhide Sheet</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Titanhide Sheet</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Primordial Hide Sheet</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Greenleaf Bundle</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Embercap Bundle</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ghostmoss Bundle</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Moonbloom Bundle</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Starspore Bundle</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Worldroot Bundle</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Faint Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Charged Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Resonant Mana Crystals (10)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arcane Prisms (10)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Astral Crystals (10)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Aetherheart Crystals (10)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Black Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Blue Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Green Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon Red Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Hatchling White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>3 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Juvenile White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>15 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Youth White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>3</td><td>8</td><td>85 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Adult White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>4</td><td>12</td><td>350 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Ancient White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>5</td><td>16</td><td>1600 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Arch Dragon White Dragon Scales (5)</td><td>6</td><td>20</td><td>11000 gp</td><td>0.2</td></tr></tbody></table></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00006","name":"Crafting in the Workbench","type":"text","sort":600000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Crafting in the Workbench</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><ol><li>Choose the party, drop a supported base item into Craft, and select its recipe, Core material and Tier.</li><li>Add one lead artisan. Every supported recipe can be crafted solo. Additional material specialists unlock their eligible Marks and combinations rather than access to the base item.</li><li>Choose Marks and compatible Anchors. Review materials, Capacity and required progress.</li><li>Create the project to reserve Party Stash stock. Reservations prevent promising the same stock to multiple projects; they do not consume it.</li><li>Commit downtime and resolve Work Blocks. At completion, review and confirm the resource consumption and finished item.</li></ol><h2>Working together</h2><p>Up to six distinct artisans contribute. Each spends the same calendar downtime. A successful one-day block produces one Progress per artisan: six artisans produce six Progress. For a block of D days (1–5), success gives D Progress per artisan; critical success gives ceiling(1.5 × D); failure gives zero for one day or floor(D ÷ 2) for longer blocks; critical failure gives zero. Time estimates assume success.</p><p>Cancel a project to release unspent reservations. Archive finished projects to keep the list manageable. Deleting a record does not refund spent materials. Report a missing finished item to the GM rather than crafting a duplicate.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00007","name":"Artisan Marks & activations","type":"text","sort":700000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Artisan Marks &amp; activations</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Click an artisan to choose Marks. Sources identify the profession and specialisation. Item compatibility, Anchors, minimum Tiers, stock and stacking rules still apply; extra artisans do not automatically activate every synergy.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Grade</th><th>Capacity cost</th><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Minor</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Standard</td><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Major</td><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Superior</td><td>3</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Mark is allowed per item. Capacity is shared across all artisans. Secondary structural material must normally be at least Core Tier minus two. Some Marks impose stricter requirements.</p><p>Make & Marks on the finished item records the Core, applied Marks and makers. Chat badges provide compact provenance. Structure-only and consumable-only Marks do not appear in the equipment picker.</p><p>Some numerical effects are automated, others require their condition to be selected or resolved during play. For explicit action costs, Add Mark Actions to Wielder creates native action entries on the owning character. These post the rules; they do not automatically resolve targets, damage or limited uses. An unspecified action cost is not permission to activate for free. Remove a linked action when its item is lost or transferred.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00008","name":"Gathering & disassembly","type":"text","sort":800000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Gathering &amp; disassembly</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><h2>Gather</h2><p>Use the Workbench Gather tab. Select a character, environment and resource; review its Tier, skill, DC, time and expected yield, then attempt the check. Region and environment can restrict available goods. Rewards go to the party or gathering character according to your campaign settings.</p><h2>Disassemble</h2><p>Drop a Wrathmaker-formatted item from your sheet or Party Stash into Disassemble. Review returns before confirming: the item is destroyed. Default recovery is 90%, rounded down separately for each material, Tier and variant. Recorded items use their project ledger; other compatible items show a standard-recipe estimate. Returns go to the selected Party Stash. Dismantled items cannot be salvaged twice or recovered as missing outputs.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00009","name":"Flanking","type":"text","sort":900000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Flanking</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>First establish a normal opposite-side flank with two qualifying melee combatants in reach. Additional qualifying combatants can contribute from other sides.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Qualifying combatants</th><th>Final target AC penalty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>−2: Off-guard (Flanked)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>−3: Outnumbered (Flanked)</td></tr><tr><td>4 or more</td><td>−4: Surrounded (Flanked)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are final penalties, not additions to the normal −2. Only qualifying melee attacks benefit; ranged attacks do not inherit this flanking penalty. Reach weapons count when they can reach the target. A creature unable to flank or an immune target follows its normal restrictions.</p><p>If the target is more than one size category larger than the largest qualifying flanker, the enhanced thresholds become six for −3 and eight for −4. A normal two-person flank still gives −2.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00010","name":"Party travel & exploration","type":"text","sort":1000000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Party travel &amp; exploration</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>The party's Exploration tab combines normal exploration activities with travel setup, rider assignments and the daily plan. On foot, the slowest member limits shared Speed. Vehicle riders use transport Speed, while walkers can still slow the group. Pulled transport uses the slowest selected hauler, subject to the vehicle limit.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Shared Speed</th><th>Activities per day</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10 feet or less</td><td>½ (one activity over two days)</td></tr><tr><td>15–25 feet</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>30–40 feet</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>45–55 feet</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>60 feet or more</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Assign Travel, Reconnoiter, Fortify Camp, Map the Area, Subsist or Other and mark activities Used as they finish. Save Travel Plan preserves choices; Begin Day & Share posts the plan. The sun button starts a new day.</p><h2>Express Rider house rule</h2><p>Select the character rolling Nature, pulling creatures and up to six affected party travellers, including walkers. The check uses the highest selected Will DC. Success or critical success increases affected overland Speeds by half for that day. Unaffected walkers and vehicle limits still constrain the group. This changes overland travel, not encounter Speed.</p></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00011","name":"Blacksmithing — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Blacksmithing — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-tempered-construction\"><h4>Tempered Construction</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+10% item HP and +1 Hardness.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-perfect-balance\"><h4>Perfect Balance</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 1 where sensible; weapon gains +1 Artisan bonus to one chosen Athletics manoeuvre made with it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-reinforced-edge\"><h4>Reinforced Edge</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+1 damage per weapon damage die against objects/Hardness; +2 per die at T5+.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-fortified-frame\"><h4>Fortified Frame</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Armour or shield gains +2 Hardness and +20% item HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-universal-master-reforge\"><h4>Master Reforge</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Recover 75% of ordinary/resource components when rebuilding and preserve compatible Wrathmaker work where physically possible.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div><h2>Hellforging</h2><p>Infernal weapons and armour shaped through fear, flame, sacrifice, and battle-tested tempers.</p><h3>Signature — Infernal Temper</h3><p>Create Hellforged equipment built around fire, blood, fear, retaliation and dangerous power.</p><h3>Mastery — Furnace Without Mercy</h3><p>Reduce Hellforging special-resource cost by 20%; at high tier recover 50% of rare infernal components from dismantled Hellforged gear.</p><h3>Legacy — Infernal Foundry</h3><p>Supports elite army weapons, infernal siege ammunition and intimidating military infrastructure.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-ember-temper\"><h4>Ember Temper</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Weapon sheds controllable light; on a critical hit deal extra fire damage equal to Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-blood-temper\"><h4>Blood Temper</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>While at or below half HP, deal +2 damage; +4 at Core T5+.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-hellfire-channel\"><h4>Hellfire Channel</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once per encounter for 1 minute, weapon deals +1d6 fire at T2–3, +2d6 at T4–5, +3d6 at T6; half ignores fire resistance.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-tormentors-edge\"><h4>Tormentor&#39;s Edge</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Critical hits force a Will save vs wielder DC; failure frightened 1, critical failure frightened 2.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-perfected-killing-edge\"><h4>Executioner&#39;s Ember</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>A weapon deals +2d6 precision damage against a creature at or below half its maximum HP, increasing to +3d6 at Core Tier 6. Select the Mark condition only for an eligible target. Precision immunity applies; this grants no attack bonus.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-1-soul-burned-steel\"><h4>Soul-Burned Steel</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day when wielder would reach 0 HP, remain at 1 HP and immediately Step then Strike; afterwards become drained 1 until daily preparations.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Hellforging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div><h2>Radiant Forging</h2><p>Protective and cleansing equipment that channels light, healing, and defence of others.</p><h3>Signature — Radiant Temper</h3><p>Create protective, cleansing and celestial equipment, especially effective against undead, fiends and corruption.</p><h3>Mastery — Purified Forge</h3><p>Reduce sacred/celestial resource waste by 20% and improve repairs to Radiant equipment.</p><h3>Legacy — Beacon Works</h3><p>Supports hospitals, temples, settlement wards, anti-undead defences and sacred military equipment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-consecrated-finish\"><h4>Consecrated Finish</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Item counts as sanctified for campaign interactions and grants +1 Artisan bonus to identify undead/fiends while worn or wielded.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-dawnbound\"><h4>Dawnbound</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Weapon deals +1 spirit damage per weapon damage die to undead and fiends.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-guardians-radiance\"><h4>Guardian&#39;s Radiance</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once per round when an adjacent ally takes damage, reduce it by 2 + Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-aegis-of-dawn\"><h4>Aegis of Dawn</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Wearer gains permanent Max HP equal to 4 × Core Tier and +1 resistance to spirit/void damage per Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-martyrs-forge\"><h4>Martyr&#39;s Forge</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Reaction once/encounter: take damage equal to twice your level to reduce damage to an ally within 15 ft by four times your level.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-2-solar-ascension\"><h4>Solar Ascension</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute, 20-ft aura: allies gain +1 Artisan bonus to AC and saves; undead/fiends take spirit damage equal to twice Core Tier at start of their turns.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Radiant Forging · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div><h2>Azlanti Artifice</h2><p>Ancient magitek, reverse-engineered machinery, original devices, and advanced infrastructure.</p><h3>Signature — Lost Artifice</h3><p>Reverse-engineer ancient technology, repair magitek and invent designs beyond normal PF2e equipment lists.</p><h3>Mastery — Reverse Engineering</h3><p>Preserve the original device while producing a reusable blueprint; repeat builds take 25% less downtime.</p><h3>Legacy — Arcane Industrialisation</h3><p>Enables automated workshops, magical power, transport, constructs and advanced siege technology.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-diagnostic-matrix\"><h4>Diagnostic Matrix</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Item reports its condition; +2 Artisan bonus to Repair and Identify checks involving it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-integrated-conduit\"><h4>Integrated Conduit</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Item can house one Mana or Aetherglass component without increasing ordinary component Bulk/space.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-adaptive-configuration\"><h4>Adaptive Configuration</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Choose two approved configurations at creation; one Interact action switches between them, such as damage type, weapon mode or tool function.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-arcane-mechanism\"><h4>Arcane Mechanism</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Add one once-per-encounter activated ability roughly appropriate to the item&#39;s tier/level and theme.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 1 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-phase-mechanism\"><h4>Phase Mechanism</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter, wielder Steps or Strides up to half Speed through creatures and non-magical obstacles as if incorporeal; must end in open space.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"blacksmithing-specialty-3-reality-engine\"><h4>Reality Engine</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute, item can maintain two mutually exclusive configurations simultaneously or ignore one normal activation prerequisite approved at creation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Blacksmithing — Azlanti Artifice · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, mechanism, fittings, frame. 2 material unit(s): metal.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00012","name":"Alchemy — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1200000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Alchemy — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-stable-formula\"><h4>Stable Formula</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · consumable</p><p>Consumable remains potent twice as long and ignores the first normal environmental spoilage event.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-efficient-batch\"><h4>Efficient Batch</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · project</p><p>Produce +10% doses, rounded down; minimum +1 when crafting 4+ items.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-refined-reagent\"><h4>Refined Reagent</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · consumable</p><p>Increase one non-attack numerical consumable effect by 10%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-quick-preparation\"><h4>Quick Preparation</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · project</p><p>Reduce batch downtime by 20%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-universal-catalyst-reserve\"><h4>Catalyst Reserve</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · project</p><p>When used as a component in another project, reduce one secondary resource requirement by 10%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div><h2>Grand Apothecary</h2><p>Refined potions and elixirs tailored for stability, duration, delivery, or specialised outcomes.</p><h3>Signature — Refined Formula</h3><p>Customise medicines, potions and elixirs for potency, duration, administration and recovery.</p><h3>Mastery — Batch Distillation</h3><p>Produce 25% more doses from the same material input.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Apothecary</h3><p>Supports hospitals, military medicine, plague response and settlement recovery.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-measured-dose\"><h4>Measured Dose</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · consumable</p><p>Remove one minor drawback or reduce a fixed consumable drawback by 25%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-concentrated\"><h4>Concentrated</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · consumable</p><p>Increase healing or temporary HP from the consumable by 25%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-extended-formula\"><h4>Extended Formula</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>Double a duration of 1 minute or longer, maximum 24 hours unless the GM approves more.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-rapid-infusion\"><h4>Rapid Infusion</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · consumable</p><p>Draw and drink/administer this consumable as a single action.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-restorative-panacea\"><h4>Restorative Panacea</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>In addition to normal effect, reduce two of clumsy, enfeebled, frightened, sickened or stupefied by 1 and attempt one counteract check vs poison/disease/curse.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-1-phoenix-draught\"><h4>Phoenix Draught</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Once/day per creature, if consumed while above 0 HP it remains active for 1 hour; first time the creature would fall to 0 HP, it instead remains at 1 HP and gains temp HP equal to 3 × Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Grand Apothecary · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div><h2>Venomcraft</h2><p>Custom toxins shaped around delivery, persistence, concealment, onset, or a chosen quarry.</p><h3>Signature — Toxin Refinement</h3><p>Customise poisons by delivery, onset, target profile, stages and concealment.</p><h3>Mastery — Venom Harvesting</h3><p>Gain 25% more usable poison material from venomous creatures and reduce poison resource cost by 15%.</p><h3>Legacy — Master Toxicologist</h3><p>Supports antivenom, pest control, military toxins and intelligence operations.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-masked-toxin\"><h4>Masked Toxin</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · project</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to the poison&#39;s DC against attempts to detect it before exposure.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-adhesive-poison\"><h4>Adhesive Poison</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>A failed Strike does not consume an applied injury poison; it remains until a successful Strike or the encounter ends.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-swift-venom\"><h4>Swift Venom</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>Reduce onset by one step; if no onset, failed initial save immediately applies Stage 1 before normal progression.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-predator-formula\"><h4>Predator Formula</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>Choose one creature family when crafted; poison DC gains +2 Artisan bonus against that family.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-mutagenic-venom\"><h4>Mutagenic Venom</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Add one approved Stage 3 rider such as slowed 1, stupefied 2 or enfeebled 2 for 1 round.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-2-perfect-killer\"><h4>Perfect Killer</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Poison gains +1 DC beyond its normal item/tier DC and treats the first successful save against it as a failure once per target.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Venomcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div><h2>Transmutative Alchemy</h2><p>Controlled material conversion and the creation of specialist composite substances.</p><h3>Signature — Material Transmutation</h3><p>Convert resource families and create composite materials for other artisans.</p><h3>Mastery — The Great Work</h3><p>Standard conversion is 2 units into 1 equal-tier unit; mastered high-tier conversions can improve to 3 into 2.</p><h3>Legacy — Transmutation Industry</h3><p>Converts surplus Kingdom resources and enables specialised industrial projects.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-purified-matrix\"><h4>Purified Matrix</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · project</p><p>Remove one undesirable mundane tag or impurity from a component.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-alchemical-alloy\"><h4>Alchemical Alloy</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · project</p><p>Component gains one approved material tag from a second same-tier material used in its creation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-composite-matrix\"><h4>Composite Matrix</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>Component can satisfy two compatible resource-family requirements while occupying one component position.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-refined-substance\"><h4>Refined Substance</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>For one named Artisan Mark, treat this component as 1 Tier higher, maximum effective T6; does not raise Core progression.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 1 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-philosophers-matrix\"><h4>Philosopher&#39;s Matrix</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Once per project, substitute one missing non-unique resource family with equal quantity of another same-tier family.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"alchemy-specialty-3-living-transmutation\"><h4>Living Transmutation</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>During daily preparations choose one of two pre-built material identities for the component; switch its native tags and compatible specialist hooks until next preparations.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Alchemy — Transmutative Alchemy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, reagent, catalyst, lining. 2 material unit(s): herbs.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00013","name":"Enchanting — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1300000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Enchanting — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-stable-matrix\"><h4>Stable Matrix</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus when resisting suppression/counteraction of the item&#39;s custom magic.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-attuned-craft\"><h4>Attuned Craft</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Key custom activations to a wielder, tradition, deity, element or other approved identity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-resonant-channel\"><h4>Resonant Channel</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+1 charge to one custom daily charge pool, maximum +1 from this Mark.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-efficient-activation\"><h4>Efficient Activation</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Once per encounter, reduce one approved 2-action custom item activation to 1 action.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-universal-arcane-safeguard\"><h4>Arcane Safeguard</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Reduce damage/penalties from a custom item overload or critical activation failure by 50%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Aethercasting</h2><p>Controlled magical enhancements and the incremental upgrading of empowered items.</p><h3>Signature — Empowerment</h3><p>Create statistic-enhancing and magically sustained equipment that can intentionally push beyond ordinary PF2e ceilings.</p><h3>Mastery — Aether Refinement</h3><p>Upgrade an existing Empowerment by paying only the material difference and half normal upgrade downtime.</p><h3>Legacy — Permanent Enchantment</h3><p>Supports wards, magical utilities, powered workshops and settlement infrastructure.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-minor-empowerment\"><h4>Minor Empowerment</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to one narrow skill use/subcategory agreed at creation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-focused-empowerment\"><h4>Focused Empowerment</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to one selected secondary statistic such as initiative, a skill, or a specific save against one effect family.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-twin-empowerment\"><h4>Twin Empowerment</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Choose two different secondary statistics; each gains +1 Artisan bonus while attuned.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-overcharged-matrix\"><h4>Overcharged Matrix</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter for 1 round, increase one existing Artisan numerical bonus on the item by +1.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-overlord-matrix\"><h4>Overlord Matrix</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Choose weapon attack or spell attack/DC when crafted; gain +1 beyond Core progression in that category. Does not stack with another Over-Potency effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-1-aetherheart-lattice\"><h4>Aetherheart Lattice</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Gain 2 charges/day; spend 1 to refresh one once-per-encounter Standard/Major activation on the item, or at start of turn gain temp HP equal to 2 × Core Tier if below half HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Aethercasting · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Essencebinding</h2><p>Approved item traits and harvested essences bound safely into qualifying equipment.</p><h3>Signature — Bind Essence</h3><p>Add traits and supernatural creature/material properties the base item does not normally possess.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Binding</h3><p>Higher-tier work supports stronger creature-derived properties and more complex essence interactions.</p><h3>Legacy — Essence Workshops</h3><p>Converts monster, planar and environmental essences into reusable crafting components.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-minor-binding\"><h4>Minor Binding</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Add one non-combat descriptive/material trait or approved utility tag.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-bound-trait\"><h4>Bound Trait</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Add one approved item/weapon trait such as shove, trip, disarm, modular or versatile.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-elemental-essence\"><h4>Elemental Essence</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Weapon deals +1d6 acid/cold/electricity/fire at T2–3, +2d6 at T4–5, +3d6 at T6; defensive items instead grant resistance equal to 2 × Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-predatory-essence\"><h4>Predatory Essence</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Bind one source-derived sense or movement mode such as scent 30 ft, climb 15 ft, swim 20 ft or darkvision.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-greater-binding\"><h4>Greater Binding</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Add one strong source-derived property such as reach extension, a once-per-encounter special attack, or comparable extraordinary trait approved by GM.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-2-living-essence\"><h4>Living Essence</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute the item awakens and manifests one high-tier transformation/ability based on the bound essence.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Essencebinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Runecarving</h2><p>Efficient rune creation, upgrading, transfer, and linked Rune Echoes.</p><h3>Signature — Runic Logic</h3><p>Build persistent sigils and linked magical logic into equipment; this replaces the old assumption that normal PF2e property runes still exist.</p><h3>Mastery — Rune Resonance</h3><p>Linked sigils are easier to upgrade and can interact across paired items.</p><h3>Legacy — Runic Infrastructure</h3><p>Supports ward arrays, military sigils and public magical systems.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-runic-signature\"><h4>Runic Signature</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify, repair or modify sigils made by this artisan.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-resonant-pair\"><h4>Resonant Pair</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Link two crafted items; while within 30 ft each bearer gains +1 Artisan bonus to saves against effects created by the other&#39;s current target.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-layered-inscription\"><h4>Layered Inscription</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Choose one Standard Mark on the item; it can be toggled between two pre-defined modes during daily preparations.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-runic-feedback\"><h4>Runic Feedback</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter when a linked weapon critically hits, paired item grants +2 Artisan bonus to its next attack, save or activation check before end of next turn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 1 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-living-rune\"><h4>Living Rune</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>One Major-or-lower custom effect on the item may switch between two equal-power versions with a single action once per encounter.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"enchanting-specialty-3-grand-glyph\"><h4>Grand Glyph</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day place a 15-ft rune zone for 1 minute that reproduces one approved Standard/Major defensive or offensive item effect for allies/enemies in the area.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Enchanting — Runecarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, lens, frame. 2 material unit(s): mana-crystals, stone.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00014","name":"Leatherwork — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1400000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Leatherwork — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-flexible-construction\"><h4>Flexible Construction</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Reduce one movement-related armour penalty by 1 where applicable.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-perfect-fit\"><h4>Supple Gussets</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to Acrobatics checks to Squeeze. It does not reduce the item&#39;s Bulk.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-reinforced-hide\"><h4>Tanner&#39;s Acid Ward</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants acid resistance equal to Core Tier. The hide is treated to shed corrosive secretions; this does not grant item HP or Hardness.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-weather-seal\"><h4>Weather Seal</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Wearer gains +2 Artisan bonus to saves/checks against ordinary environmental exposure covered by the garment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-universal-adaptive-strapping\"><h4>Adaptive Strapping</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Once per round drawing/stowing one item secured to the gear is part of the same Interact action used to manipulate it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div><h2>Wyrmcraft</h2><p>Dragon-scale equipment that preserves an adaptation belonging to the source dragon.</p><h3>Signature — Draconic Essence</h3><p>Preserve and exploit qualities from dragon type, colour and age in armour, weapons and reinforcement. Dragon Scale Core and Reinforcement already provide native colour resistance; Wyrmcraft deepens or transforms that inheritance.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Harvest</h3><p>Gain more usable dragon material and reduce waste while preparing scales and hides.</p><h3>Legacy — Dragonworks</h3><p>Creates elite army equipment, prestige goods, diplomatic trophies and draconic settlement works.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-wyrm-inscription\"><h4>Wyrm Inscription</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Item visibly records source dragon; +2 Artisan bonus to identify or track lore tied to that dragon type.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-draconic-resistance\"><h4>Draconic Resistance</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Requires Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement. Increase the item&#39;s active native resistance by Dragon Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-scale-dominion\"><h4>Scale Dominion</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Armour/shield gains +2 Hardness and +15 HP per Dragon Tier; weapon instead ignores resistance equal to Dragon Tier against the associated damage type.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-draconic-constitution\"><h4>Draconic Constitution</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>While attuned to worn armour, gain Max HP equal to 4 × Dragon Tier and a +2 Artisan bonus to saves against effects that deal the associated damage type; Green applies to poison effects. This replaces the Mark&#39;s former extra resistance.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-wyrms-fury\"><h4>Wyrm&#39;s Fury</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Weapon gains +1 additional base weapon damage die beyond Core progression. Must use Dragon Scale Core or Reinforcement; does not stack with other Over-Striking.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-1-dragonheart-awakening\"><h4>Dragonheart Awakening</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute gain fly Speed equal to land Speed, increase the active native resistance by 2 × Dragon Tier, and gain one 30-ft cone breath weapon dealing 2d6 per Dragon Tier, basic Reflex save. This increase stacks with Draconic Resistance on the same item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Wyrmcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div><h2>Beastbinding</h2><p>Prepared hides that preserve a useful natural quality of the creature they came from.</p><h3>Signature — Preserve the Beast</h3><p>Retain a natural or supernatural quality from the creature whose hide/material was used.</p><h3>Mastery — Master Harvester</h3><p>Improve creature-material yield and preserve delicate traits that ordinary harvesting would destroy.</p><h3>Legacy — Monstercraft Trade</h3><p>Turns rare creature materials into specialist exports and campaign resources.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-trophy-memory\"><h4>Trophy Memory</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to Recall Knowledge about the source creature family while carrying/wearing the item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-predators-sense\"><h4>Predator&#39;s Sense</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Gain one source-appropriate sense such as scent 15 ft, low-light vision, or +2 Artisan bonus to tracking that creature family.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-natural-movement\"><h4>Natural Movement</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Gain one source-appropriate movement mode: climb 15 ft, swim 20 ft, or +10 ft Speed in a defined natural environment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-apex-hide\"><h4>Apex Hide</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>At start of combat gain temp HP equal to 3 × Core Tier and +1 Artisan bonus to saves against one source-creature theme such as fear, cold, poison or grabs.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-apex-trait\"><h4>Apex Trait</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Gain one extraordinary source-derived trait/ability such as powerful leap, amphibious movement, tremorsense 15 ft, or comparable effect approved by GM.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-2-chimera-binding\"><h4>Chimera Binding</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Combine two compatible creature-source properties in one item; choose which is active as a free action once per round, or activate both for 1 minute once/day.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Beastbinding · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div><h2>Mantlecraft</h2><p>Prestigious and protective mantles, cloaks, robes, and environmental garments.</p><h3>Signature — Great Mantles</h3><p>Create exceptional cloaks, coats, ceremonial furs and environmental garments.</p><h3>Mastery — Luxury Craftsmanship</h3><p>Reduce rare-fur waste and substantially increase trade/prestige value.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Clothier</h3><p>Supports diplomacy, gifts, court prestige and luxury industry.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-trophy-finish\"><h4>Trophy Finish</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to social checks where the displayed trophy/source is relevant to status or intimidation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-weather-mantle\"><h4>Whiteout Mantle</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants cold resistance equal to twice Core Tier. It does not confer immunity to weather, difficult terrain, or environmental penalties.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-predators-cloak\"><h4>Predator&#39;s Cloak</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Stealth and Survival in one source-appropriate terrain; once/encounter Step 5 ft after successfully Hiding.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-court-mantle\"><h4>Court Mantle</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Diplomacy and Society in formal settings; adjacent allies gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves against fear while wearer is conscious.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 1 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-sovereign-pelt\"><h4>Dread Sovereign Pelt</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants a +3 untyped Artisan bonus to Intimidation and a +2 untyped Artisan bonus to Survival. It grants no maximum HP. The trophy declares its wearer a hunter worthy of fear.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"leatherwork-specialty-3-legendary-pelt\"><h4>Legendary Pelt</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute manifest one major supernatural trait of the source creature, such as invisibility, huge leap, elemental aura or transformation approved by GM.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Leatherwork — Mantlecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, grip, strap, straps, backing, lining, wrap, cover. 2 material unit(s): leather, dragon-scale.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00015","name":"Carpentry — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1500000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Carpentry — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-seasoned-construction\"><h4>Seasoned Construction</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Wooden item ignores normal warping/weathering and gains +10% item HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-light-frame\"><h4>Light Frame</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 1 where the wooden frame is a meaningful portion of the item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-precision-joinery\"><h4>Precision Joinery</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to checks to Repair, maintain or operate its crafted mechanism.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-reinforced-limb\"><h4>Skyhunter Limbs</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>A ranged weapon deals additional damage equal to Core Tier against an airborne target. Select the Mark condition only when the target is flying or falling. This is not bonus damage against objects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-universal-modular-frame\"><h4>Modular Frame</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>One approved wooden component can be swapped during daily preparations without rebuilding the entire item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div><h2>Warbowyer</h2><p>Engineered bows, crossbows, ballistae, loading systems, and specialist ammunition.</p><h3>Signature — Engineered Ranged Weapons</h3><p>Build bows, crossbows, ballistae, specialist ammunition and advanced loading mechanisms.</p><h3>Mastery — Master Fletching</h3><p>Produce ammunition efficiently and maintain engineered ranged weapons with reduced waste.</p><h3>Legacy — Missile Industry</h3><p>Improves army archers, towers, ballistae and settlement ranged defence.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-true-fletching\"><h4>True Fletching</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Ignore the first range-related environmental penalty from ordinary wind; ammunition can carry the artisan&#39;s identifying fletch.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-specialist-ammo-chamber\"><h4>Specialist Ammo Chamber</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Weapon can use one additional approved specialist ammunition family without modification.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-longshot-construction\"><h4>Longshot Construction</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Increase range increment by 50%; first range increment beyond normal maximum does not impose an additional penalty.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-rapid-mechanism\"><h4>Rapid Mechanism</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once per round reduce one reload action by 1 action, minimum 0; if already reload 0, instead gain +1 Artisan bonus to first Strike after reloading.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-perfected-tension\"><h4>Horizonstring</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>A ranged weapon grants a +2 untyped Artisan bonus to its attack rolls against targets beyond its first range increment. Select the Mark condition only for that distance. Range penalties and maximum range still apply; this is not a universal attack bonus.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-1-warbow-overdraw\"><h4>Warbow Overdraw</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +1 additional base weapon damage die beyond Core progression; on a natural 1, wielder becomes off-guard until start of next turn from the violent recoil/tension.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warbowyer · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div><h2>Masterwright</h2><p>Bridges, roads, docks, fieldworks, buildings, and major wooden structures.</p><h3>Signature — Great Works</h3><p>Build bridges, roads, palisades, docks, towers, camps and major wooden infrastructure.</p><h3>Mastery — Efficient Construction</h3><p>Reduce Lumber cost and repair downtime for qualifying projects.</p><h3>Legacy — Kingdom Builder</h3><p>Improves construction throughput, roads, fortifications, settlement expansion and repairs.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-builders-mark\"><h4>Builder&#39;s Mark</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify structural weaknesses or repair methods in wooden construction.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-reinforced-frame\"><h4>Reinforced Frame</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · structure</p><p>Structure or wooden vehicle gains +20% HP and +2 Hardness.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-rapid-assembly\"><h4>Rapid Assembly</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Reduce qualifying construction or field-fortification time by 30%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-modular-construction\"><h4>Modular Construction</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · structure</p><p>Structure can be dismantled/reconfigured while recovering 80% of ordinary materials; temporary field works can be deployed in half normal time.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-grand-design\"><h4>Grand Design</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Kingdom project using this design reduces one recurring Lumber/repair cost by 25% and gains +2 Artisan bonus to its primary construction check.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-2-citadel-framework\"><h4>Citadel Framework</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Major fortification counts as one category tougher for structural damage and grants defenders +1 Artisan bonus to checks/saves against forced entry, siege movement and collapse effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Masterwright · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div><h2>Warcarving</h2><p>Combat forms and utility carvings applied to wooden weapons, shields, and tools.</p><h3>Signature — Carved Form</h3><p>Add combat identities and totemic properties to wooden weapons, shields and tools.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Carving</h3><p>Preserve increasingly complex magical/totemic carvings without weakening the wood.</p><h3>Legacy — Carved Traditions</h3><p>Supports ceremonial weapons, military equipment and cultural relics.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-carved-grip\"><h4>Carved Grip</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to checks to resist Disarm or losing grip of the carved item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-wolf-carving\"><h4>Wolf Carving</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>After hitting a creature, gain +5 ft Speed when moving toward that creature until end of turn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-bear-carving\"><h4>Bear Carving</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>While wielding/raising item, gain resistance to physical damage equal to half Core Tier, rounded up; doubles against forced-movement damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-serpent-carving\"><h4>Serpent Carving</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Weapon gains one approved flexible/reach-style property; once/round after a successful Strike, Step 5 ft without triggering reactions from that target.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 1 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-spirit-carving\"><h4>Spirit Carving</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Item houses a totem spirit; once/encounter activate for 1 minute to gain +1 Artisan bonus to attack or AC chosen when crafted plus a themed sense/movement benefit.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"carpentry-specialty-3-totemic-ascendance\"><h4>Totemic Ascendance</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Choose Wolf, Bear, Serpent or Stag each daily preparation; item gains that totem&#39;s Major-level package for the day, without consuming additional Capacity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Carpentry — Warcarving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip. 2 material unit(s): wood.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00016","name":"Stonemasonry — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1600000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Stonemasonry — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-stonebound\"><h4>Stonebound</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Hardness and +10% item/structure HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-perfect-foundation\"><h4>Perfect Foundation</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · structure</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to checks to stabilise or repair a structure using this work.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-anchored-construction\"><h4>Anchored Construction</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · structure</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus against forced movement/toppling; structures count as one size larger for such effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-load-bearing-cut\"><h4>Load-Bearing Cut</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Increase structure/stone-component HP by 20%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-universal-resonant-stone\"><h4>Resonant Stone</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Component gains one `ward`, `arcane-anchor` or equivalent approved tag for compatible specialist work.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Megalithics</h2><p>Monumental works, fortresses, roads, aqueducts, walls, and major civil structures.</p><h3>Signature — Great Works</h3><p>Create fortresses, roads, aqueducts, monumental walls, towers and vast stone projects.</p><h3>Mastery — Monumental Engineering</h3><p>Reduce Stone waste and repair time for major works.</p><h3>Legacy — Civilisation Builder</h3><p>Transforms settlements through enduring infrastructure and wonders.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-masons-seal\"><h4>Mason&#39;s Seal</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify damage, load paths and original construction methods in stone works.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-enduring-monument\"><h4>Enduring Monument</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · structure</p><p>Structure gains +25% HP and +2 Hardness.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-grand-foundation\"><h4>Grand Foundation</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · structure</p><p>Structures built on this foundation gain +2 Artisan bonus against collapse, subsidence and siege movement; repairs restore 25% more HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-civic-wonder\"><h4>Civic Wonder</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · structure</p><p>Assign one Kingdom purpose at creation—Culture, Defence, Trade, Faith or Infrastructure—and grant a strong project bonus agreed for that subsystem.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-imperial-work\"><h4>Imperial Work</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · structure</p><p>Major structure reduces one related Kingdom resource cost by 25% and counts as a landmark/wonder for prestige and strategic effects.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-1-world-rooted-foundation\"><h4>World-Rooted Foundation</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · structure</p><p>Structure cannot be moved or toppled by ordinary effects and gains resistance to siege/structural damage equal to 3 × Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Megalithics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Runemasonry</h2><p>Wardstones and enduring magical inscriptions that protect places rather than carried items.</p><h3>Signature — Wardstones</h3><p>Bind magical zones, alarms, protections and restrictions to locations rather than carried items.</p><h3>Mastery — Deep Inscription</h3><p>Increase ward area, duration and magical stability.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Wards</h3><p>Protects settlements from intrusion, teleportation, undead, weather and magical assault.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-inscribed-keystone\"><h4>Inscribed Keystone</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify/repair the ward and clearly marks ownership or purpose to authorised users.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-sentinel-rune\"><h4>Sentinel Rune</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Ward detects a chosen creature/type crossing its boundary and alerts designated recipients within the site.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-sanctuary-ward\"><h4>Sanctuary Ward</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Allies in a 20-ft zone gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves and temp HP equal to Core Tier when they first enter each encounter.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-war-rune\"><h4>War Rune</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Defenders in a 20-ft zone gain +1 Artisan bonus to attack rolls and damage equal to Core Tier on first successful Strike each round.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-fortress-sigil\"><h4>Fortress Sigil</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Large warded area suppresses hostile teleportation/forced planar entry unless attacker succeeds at a counteract/check against the ward&#39;s DC.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-2-dominion-ward\"><h4>Dominion Ward</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Choose one hostile creature family or supernatural theme; within the ward they take a -1 Artisan penalty to attacks/saves and cannot benefit from concealment against authorised defenders.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Runemasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div><h2>Titanmasonry</h2><p>Stone wargear, constructs, siege engines, and powerful Titanic forms.</p><h3>Signature — Titanic Construction</h3><p>Create stone armour, colossal shields, siege devices, constructs and crushing wargear.</p><h3>Mastery — Mountaincraft</h3><p>Make enormous stone components usable without losing impossible stability.</p><h3>Legacy — Stone Legions</h3><p>Supports constructs, fortifications and siege warfare.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-titanic-fit\"><h4>Titanic Fit</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Ignore 1 Bulk of a stone component for encumbrance while properly worn/wielded.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-anchored\"><h4>Anchored</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus against forced movement, Trip and Reposition while using the item; count as one size larger for those effects where allowed.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-earthshaker\"><h4>Earthshaker</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/round on a critical hit or successful Shield Block, adjacent enemy must save or become off-guard and knocked 5 ft; critical failure also prone.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-mountain-plate\"><h4>Basalt Bastion</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to Core Tier and a +2 untyped Artisan bonus to Fortitude saves. It no longer increases maximum HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 1 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-mountain-blood-plate\"><h4>Heart of the Mountain</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants physical resistance equal to twice Core Tier and a +3 untyped Artisan bonus to Fortitude saves, but imposes a -5-foot untyped penalty to land Speed. It grants no maximum HP. Physical resistances do not add together.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"stonemason-specialty-3-living-colossus\"><h4>Living Colossus</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute increase size by one category, gain +5 ft reach, +2 Artisan bonus to Athletics and physical resistance equal to Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Stonemasonry — Titanmasonry · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, frame, fittings, lens. 2 material unit(s): stone.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00017","name":"Glassmaking — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1700000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Glassmaking — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-perfect-clarity\"><h4>Perfect Clarity</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to visual Perception checks made through the crafted optic.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-hardened-glass\"><h4>Glarecut Glass</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>While holding this focus, gain a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to Perception checks to Seek visually. It filters glare without granting immunity to dazzled or concealed.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-arcane-lens\"><h4>Arcane Lens</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Item gains `arcane`, `optic`, `conductor` tags for compatible specialist Marks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-precision-focus\"><h4>Precision Focus</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to one approved ranged measurement/surveying check using the item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-universal-shatter-safe\"><h4>Shatter Safe</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>First time per day the glass component would be destroyed, it instead remains at 1 HP.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Prismcraft</h2><p>Lenses and prisms that focus, split, redirect, or transform light and magical energy.</p><h3>Signature — Arcane Optics</h3><p>Focus, split, redirect and transform light or magical energy with precision lenses and prisms.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Refraction</h3><p>Safely handle stronger magical energy and reduce material loss in advanced optical components.</p><h3>Legacy — Observatory Craft</h3><p>Supports surveying, astronomy, navigation, signalling and watchtowers.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-calibrated-lens\"><h4>Surveyor&#39;s Reticle</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>While holding this focus, gain a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to initiative rolls. It measures emerging lines of fire rather than repeating Glarecut Glass&#39;s Seek bonus.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-focusing-lens\"><h4>Focusing Lens</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Ranged weapon/focus increases first range increment by 25%; spell focus gains +10 ft to one approved non-area range category.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-spectrum-prism\"><h4>Spectrum Prism</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Choose two energy types at creation; once per round when dealing one, convert up to half the bonus energy damage to the other.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-beam-splitter\"><h4>Beam Splitter</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter after a ranged Strike or single-target item activation hits, repeat 50% of its bonus damage/effect against a second target within 15 ft of the first.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-trueglass-crown\"><h4>Trueglass Crown</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Wearer gains constant see-invisibility-style perception within 30 ft and +2 Artisan bonus to checks/saves against visual illusions and concealment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-1-crown-prism\"><h4>Sovereign Refraction</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>A held spell focus grants a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to spell DC and a +2 untyped Artisan bonus to Arcana, but imposes a -1 untyped penalty to spell attacks. Requires a Tier 5+ optical Anchor. Multiple copies do not multiply the penalty. It is a save-spell specialist, not a second Overlord Matrix.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Prismcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Mirrorcraft</h2><p>Reflective magic, illusions, scrying, communication, and linked mirrors.</p><h3>Signature — Reflection</h3><p>Create supernatural mirrors for illusion, scrying, communication, defence and travel.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Reflection</h3><p>Safely reflect or retain increasingly powerful magical phenomena.</p><h3>Legacy — Mirror Network</h3><p>Links settlements for communication, intelligence and eventually transport.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-perfect-reflection\"><h4>Perfect Reflection</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Mirror retains flawless clarity and grants +1 Artisan bonus to visual identification or disguise checks using it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-truth-mirror\"><h4>Truth Mirror</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to checks to detect visual disguises, glamours and shape-changing seen in the mirror.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-reflective-ward\"><h4>Reflective Ward</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Reaction once/encounter when targeted by a spell attack: gain +2 Artisan bonus to AC against it; if the attack critically misses, redirect a reduced version at an eligible target within 30 ft.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-doppelglass\"><h4>Doppelglass</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter create a reflected duplicate until start of next turn, granting concealed against the next attack that targets you.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-gate-mirror\"><h4>Gate Mirror</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Pair with another crafted Gate Mirror; once/day transport willing creatures through the linked mirrors subject to GM-set distance/Kingdom infrastructure limits.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-2-mirror-lord\"><h4>Mirror Lord</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute, first hostile spell or ranged magical effect each round targeting wearer can be contested with a counteract-style check; success negates, critical success reflects it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Mirrorcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Aetherglass</h2><p>Mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry, construct cores, and powered components.</p><h3>Signature — Mana Conduction</h3><p>Build mana batteries, spell reservoirs, magical circuitry and construct cores.</p><h3>Mastery — Aether Cells</h3><p>Store progressively greater magical energy with less loss and safer discharge.</p><h3>Legacy — Arcane Grid</h3><p>Powers large-scale magical infrastructure and magitek networks.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-stable-cell\"><h4>Stable Cell</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Stored magical charge does not decay under ordinary downtime/environmental conditions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-mana-reservoir\"><h4>Mana Reservoir</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Item gains 1 charge/day usable by one listed custom activation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-arcane-conductor\"><h4>Arcane Conductor</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Increase one magical damage/healing effect generated by the item by +1 die; if effect has no dice, increase fixed value by 25%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-overflow-channel\"><h4>Overflow Channel</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter overcharge one activation: +50% range or +1 damage/healing die, but item loses 1 additional charge if it has charges.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 1 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-crystal-matrix\"><h4>Crystal Matrix</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Reduce the Capacity cost of one compatible Enchanting or Azlanti Artifice Mark on the same item by 1, minimum 1; the item still cannot exceed the Capacity granted by its Core Tier unless another explicit effect raises that maximum.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"glassmaking-specialty-3-eternity-cell\"><h4>Eternity Cell</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Item gains 3 charges/day and recovers 1 expended charge the first time each encounter the wearer critically succeeds at a relevant attack/save/activation check.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Glassmaking — Aetherglass · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lens, catalyst, core. 2 material unit(s): stone, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00018","name":"Pottery — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1800000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Pottery — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-hardened-ceramic\"><h4>Emberproof Glaze</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Worn armor or a held shield grants fire resistance 1. Multiple sources use only the highest applicable resistance.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-thermal-craft\"><h4>Thermal Craft</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Container/component safely handles extreme mundane heat/cold.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-sealed-vessel\"><h4>Sealed Vessel</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Contents do not leak, evaporate or contaminate through ordinary damage until the vessel is Broken.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-shock-fired\"><h4>Shock-Fired</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus against effects that would shatter or rupture the ceramic item.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-universal-nested-chamber\"><h4>Nested Chamber</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Creates one concealed internal compartment or secondary reagent chamber.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Ceramancy</h2><p>Living clay, terracotta constructs, ceramic armour, figurines, and guardians.</p><h3>Signature — Living Clay</h3><p>Create supernatural ceramics, terracotta guardians and adaptive ceramic armour.</p><h3>Mastery — Awakened Kiln</h3><p>Build increasingly complex animated ceramics with less breakage and better control.</p><h3>Legacy — Terracotta Works</h3><p>Supports workers, guardians, soldiers and settlement sentinels.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-fired-seal\"><h4>Fired Seal</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to identify or repair the ceramic component and its maker&#39;s construction pattern.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-ceramic-plate\"><h4>Ceramic Plate</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Armour component gains +2 Hardness and +15 HP per Core Tier without increasing Bulk.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-living-clay\"><h4>Living Clay</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>At start of wearer&#39;s turn, repair the item itself for HP equal to Core Tier if it is not Destroyed.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-terracotta-guardian\"><h4>Terracotta Guardian</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/day animate a small guardian/figurine for 10 minutes; use a GM-approved creature profile appropriate to item tier, primarily defensive/support focused.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-adaptive-ceramic\"><h4>Adaptive Ceramic</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/round when struck by physical damage, choose bludgeoning/piercing/slashing; gain resistance equal to 2 × Core Tier against that type until start of next turn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-1-living-ceramic-shell\"><h4>Living Ceramic Shell</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Worn armour grants regenerating temp HP equal to 2 × Core Tier at start of each turn if wearer has none; also repairs itself for same amount.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Ceramancy · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Reliquarycraft</h2><p>Vessels that preserve blessings, curses, spirits, essences, and planar energy.</p><h3>Signature — Vessel of Essence</h3><p>Capture and safely preserve supernatural essences, spirits, curses, blessings and planar energy.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Containment</h3><p>Safely house stronger and more volatile essences with less risk of leakage or corruption.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Reliquaries</h3><p>Supports temples, magical institutions, cursed-artifact storage and spirit containment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-sanctified-vessel\"><h4>Sanctified Vessel</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to checks to identify the contained essence and prevents ordinary spiritual leakage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-essence-vessel\"><h4>Essence Vessel</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Safely stores one harvested supernatural essence for later crafting without degradation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-bound-spirit\"><h4>Bound Spirit</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>House one willing/controlled spirit; item can grant one minor sense, Lore or once/day guidance effect tied to that spirit.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-sealed-curse\"><h4>Sealed Curse</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Contain one curse/hazard effect; while sealed it cannot spread normally and grants +2 Artisan bonus to counteract/manage it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-release-matrix\"><h4>Release Matrix</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day deliberately discharge stored essence as a powerful item activation appropriate to the source; vessel then requires recharging/refilling.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-2-grand-reliquary\"><h4>Grand Reliquary</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Safely maintain up to three compatible essences and switch the active one during daily preparations; once/day combine two for one Synergy-style activation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Reliquarycraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Pyroceramics</h2><p>Crucibles, bomb casings, heat-resistant vessels, magical kilns, and industrial ceramics.</p><h3>Signature — Cruciblecraft</h3><p>Create bomb casings, furnaces, crucibles, pressure vessels and extreme-temperature components.</p><h3>Mastery — Grand Kiln</h3><p>Improve industrial/alchemical throughput and reduce failures when processing extreme heat materials.</p><h3>Legacy — Industrial Kilns</h3><p>Supports bricks, pipes, sanitation, forges, alchemy and mass production.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-heatproof-glaze\"><h4>Heatproof Glaze</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Container/component ignores ordinary heat damage and gains +2 Artisan bonus against thermal breakage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-thermal-crucible\"><h4>Thermal Crucible</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>When used by another artisan processing heat-sensitive material, reduce material loss by 10%.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-fragmenting-casing\"><h4>Fragmenting Casing</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Increase bomb/splash item&#39;s splash radius by 5 ft and splash damage by Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-shaped-charge\"><h4>Shaped Charge</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Explosive item can trade splash radius for force: against one target/object deal +1 damage die per two Core Tiers, rounded up.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 1 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-pressure-vessel\"><h4>Pressure Vessel</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Increase one explosive/alchemical item&#39;s primary damage by 50%; on a critical crafting failure during manufacture, complication severity is increased.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"pottery-specialty-3-furnace-heart\"><h4>Furnace Heart</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day emit a 15-ft thermal eruption dealing 2d6 fire per Core Tier, basic Reflex save; item remains a qualifying portable forge/crucible for relevant downtime work.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Pottery — Pyroceramics · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, catalyst, reagent. 2 material unit(s): stone, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00019","name":"Weaving — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":1900000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Weaving — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-lightweave\"><h4>Lightweave</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Reduce Bulk by 1 for primarily textile equipment.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-perfect-thread\"><h4>Perfect Thread</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to the next Tailoring/Leatherworking check using this textile as a component.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-reinforced-weave\"><h4>Slipknot Weave</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>While wearing this armor, gain a +2 untyped Artisan bonus to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape. This does not improve an unarmed attack used to Escape.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-weatherproof-weave\"><h4>Weatherproof Weave</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Wearer ignores ordinary rain/wind exposure and gains +1 Artisan bonus against severe weather.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-universal-tensioned-thread\"><h4>Tensioned Thread</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Rope, bowstring, net or sail gains +2 Artisan bonus to checks involving load, restraint or structural tension.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Aetherweaving</h2><p>Manathread and magical cloth that carry enchantments, wards, and arcane patterns.</p><h3>Signature — Manathread</h3><p>Produce magically conductive fabric capable of storing, carrying and shaping supernatural energy.</p><h3>Mastery — Arcane Loom</h3><p>Weave stronger magical fibres and exotic feedstocks without losing their properties.</p><h3>Legacy — Magical Textile Industry</h3><p>Supports magical garments, banners, specialist exports and arcane infrastructure.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-resonant-thread\"><h4>Resonant Thread</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Textile gains `mana`, `conductor`, `aetherwoven` tags and +1 Artisan bonus to checks to identify its magic.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-manaweave\"><h4>Manaweave</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Worn item gains resistance to one chosen magical energy type equal to Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-spellthread\"><h4>Spellthread</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Store one approved spell/effect in the garment, usable once/day at an item rank appropriate to Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-ethereal-weave\"><h4>Ethereal Weave</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Wearer ignores difficult terrain from non-magical ground and once/encounter Steps 10 ft through occupied spaces without triggering reactions.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-expanded-matrix\"><h4>Expanded Matrix</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Reduce one compatible Enchanting/Tailoring Mark&#39;s Capacity cost by 1, minimum 1; finished item still has hard maximum 8 Capacity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-1-aetherbound-form\"><h4>Aetherbound Form</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute garment becomes semi-ethereal: fly Speed 20 ft, resistance to physical damage equal to Core Tier, and wearer can squeeze through openings as though one size smaller.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Aetherweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Ironweaving</h2><p>Warcloth, armour backing, nets, ropes, bowstrings, sails, and resilient reinforcement.</p><h3>Signature — Warcloth</h3><p>Produce armour backing, nets, ropes, strings, sails and flexible reinforcement designed for combat stress.</p><h3>Mastery — Steel Thread</h3><p>Integrate stronger materials without sacrificing flexibility.</p><h3>Legacy — Military Textiles</h3><p>Supports armour, siege gear, sails, ropes and army equipment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-warcloth-finish\"><h4>Warcloth Finish</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+10% textile component HP and +1 Artisan bonus to checks against tearing/cutting.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-impact-mesh\"><h4>Impact Mesh</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Worn gear grants resistance 1 to physical damage per two Core Tiers, rounded up.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-flexible-weave\"><h4>Flexible Weave</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Reduce one armour movement penalty by 5 ft and improve one Dex-cap-style campaign limitation by +1 where applicable.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-shock-absorbing-warcloth\"><h4>Shock-Absorbing Warcloth</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>At start of each turn, if wearer has no temp HP, gain temp HP equal to Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-silken-steel\"><h4>Silken Steel</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Worn armour gains +1 AC beyond Core progression and physical resistance equal to Core Tier; does not stack with another Artisan AC-over-Core effect.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 4+; Core-tier Anchor required</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-2-unbreakable-braid\"><h4>Lifeline Braid</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants bleed resistance equal to twice Core Tier and a +3 untyped Artisan bonus to Athletics and Acrobatics checks to Escape. It grants no maximum HP and does not improve an unarmed Escape attack.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Ironweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Heraldweaving</h2><p>Standards, banners, and tapestries supporting morale, identity, armies, and prestige.</p><h3>Signature — Great Standards</h3><p>Create banners and tapestries that carry morale, identity and supernatural command presence.</p><h3>Mastery — Living Heraldry</h3><p>Standards grow more potent when tied to a recognised army, ruler, settlement or company.</p><h3>Legacy — National Identity</h3><p>Supports armies, festivals, loyalty, diplomacy and prestige.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-heraldic-seal\"><h4>Heraldic Seal</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to social checks proving authority, affiliation or military identity represented by the standard.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-unbroken-standard\"><h4>Unbroken Standard</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Allies within 20 ft gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves against fear while the banner is displayed.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-marching-banner\"><h4>Marching Banner</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Allies beginning turn within 20 ft gain +5 ft status-equivalent movement for that turn and ignore first 5 ft of difficult terrain.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-kings-colours\"><h4>King&#39;s Colours</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Allies within 20 ft gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves against mental effects and +1 to Aid checks involving coordinated action.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-conquerors-standard\"><h4>Conqueror&#39;s Standard</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter for 1 minute, allies in 30 ft gain +1 Artisan bonus to attack rolls after they reduce an enemy to 0 HP; bonus lasts until end of their next turn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"weaving-specialty-3-sovereign-standard\"><h4>Sovereign Standard</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>30-ft aura: allies gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves and damage equal to Core Tier on first hit each round; once/day aura also grants temp HP equal to 3 × Core Tier when activated.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Weaving — Heraldweaving · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: string, lining, backing, wrap, strap, straps, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00020","name":"Bookmaking — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":2000000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Bookmaking — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-perfect-index\"><h4>Perfect Index</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Find a known entry in the work immediately rather than spending extended search time.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-preserved-knowledge\"><h4>Preserved Knowledge</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Book/map/formula resists ordinary water, age and environmental damage.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-master-copy\"><h4>Master Copy</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Copying a formula/text from this master takes 50% less downtime.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-encoded-script\"><h4>Encoded Script</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to conceal or protect the text from unauthorised reading.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-universal-reference-tabs\"><h4>Reference Tabs</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Once per 10 minutes, gain +1 Artisan bonus to one Recall Knowledge check using the work&#39;s documented subject.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Grimoirecraft</h2><p>Living spellbooks and codices with enhanced memory, resonance, organisation, and access.</p><h3>Signature — Living Grimoires</h3><p>Create spellbooks and codices that interact directly with spell preparation, memory and magical resonance.</p><h3>Mastery — Arcane Codex</h3><p>Improve magical capacity, indexing and stability while reducing time to expand or revise the grimoire.</p><h3>Legacy — Grand Academies</h3><p>Supports magical education, spell research and institutional knowledge.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-indexed-arcana\"><h4>Indexed Arcana</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to Recall Knowledge about spells recorded in the grimoire and instantly locate any known entry.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-mnemonic-pages\"><h4>Mnemonic Pages</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Once/day during preparation, swap one prepared/recorded spell choice of an appropriate rank without needing another full preparation period.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-resonant-chapter\"><h4>Resonant Chapter</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Choose one spell trait/theme; spells of that theme gain +1 Artisan bonus to damage/healing per spell rank or +1 to one associated counteract/check, chosen at creation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-spell-echo\"><h4>Spell Echo</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter after casting a spell from/through the grimoire, repeat one non-damaging minor rider or 50% of bonus damage/healing against the same or a second valid target.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-archmage-codex\"><h4>Archmage Codex</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute choose one mode: +25% spell range, ignore resistance equal to Core Tier, or add +1 spell damage/healing die.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-1-endless-grimoire\"><h4>Endless Grimoire</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day recover one expended spell slot or equivalent spell resource of a rank no higher than half Core Tier rounded up, subject to GM conversion for non-slot casters.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grimoirecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Chroniclecraft</h2><p>Lore, formulae, techniques, and Codices of Mastery that make recorded knowledge usable.</p><h3>Signature — Codices of Mastery</h3><p>Record Lore, formulae, techniques and expertise precisely enough that others can temporarily benefit from it.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Instruction</h3><p>Preserve increasingly advanced knowledge while reducing training/research time.</p><h3>Legacy — Great Library</h3><p>Improves research, education, formula preservation and Culture.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-scholars-index\"><h4>Scholar&#39;s Index</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to research checks using the chronicle&#39;s documented subject.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-lore-codex\"><h4>Lore Codex</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>After 10 minutes study, gain trained-equivalent access to one narrow Lore for 8 hours, or +1 Artisan bonus if already trained.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-crafting-manual\"><h4>Crafting Manual</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>For one recipe/category, reduce crafting downtime by 20% and gain +2 Artisan bonus to the first project check each day.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-tactical-treatise\"><h4>Tactical Treatise</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>After study, once/encounter gain +2 Artisan bonus to one attack, save or Recall Knowledge check against the documented enemy/tactic.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-masters-testament\"><h4>Master&#39;s Testament</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>After daily study, gain temporary access to one approved feat/technique for which you meet level prerequisites until next preparations.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-2-legendary-chronicle\"><h4>Legendary Chronicle</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>During preparations choose one documented discipline; up to six readers gain +1 Artisan bonus to related skill checks and one once/day reroll in that discipline.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Chroniclecraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Grand Cartography</h2><p>Master atlases for exploration, resources, roads, armies, settlements, and expansion.</p><h3>Signature — Master Atlas</h3><p>Create maps that record resources, hazards, routes, magical phenomena and strategic terrain.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Survey</h3><p>Reveal hidden resources and improve route accuracy with less exploration time.</p><h3>Legacy — Kingdom Survey</h3><p>Improves hex claims, roads, army movement, settlement placement and resource exploitation.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-surveyors-mark\"><h4>Surveyor&#39;s Mark</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to navigation and Reconnoiter-style checks in mapped territory.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-safe-passage\"><h4>Safe Passage</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Party reduces non-combat travel delay from known mundane hazards by 25% in mapped territory.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-resource-survey\"><h4>Resource Survey</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>Map can reveal one hidden or underexploited resource site after successful survey; Kingdom extraction from it gains +1 project bonus.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-strategic-map\"><h4>Strategic Map</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · project</p><p>Armies/parties using the map gain +1 Artisan bonus to initiative or strategic movement checks in the mapped region.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 1 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-hidden-paths\"><h4>Hidden Paths</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Discover or establish a secret route that reduces travel time by 25% and grants +2 Artisan bonus to avoid detection while using it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"bookmaking-specialty-3-world-atlas\"><h4>World Atlas</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · project</p><p>Atlas magically updates known mapped holdings; once per Kingdom turn designate one mapped region to gain a strong temporary bonus to travel, resource extraction or settlement planning.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Bookmaking — Grand Cartography · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: core, cover, catalyst. 2 material unit(s): wood, leather, herbs, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}},{"_id":"wmGuidePage00021","name":"Tailoring — Specialisation reference","type":"text","sort":2100000,"ownership":{"default":2},"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<section class=\"cmt-rules-handbook\"><header><h1>Tailoring — Specialisation reference</h1><p>Wrathmaker · Player guide</p></header><p>Campaign descriptions, not a promise that every effect is automated. Check the current profession entry for any local changes.</p><h2>Universal Artisan Marks</h2><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-perfect-fit\"><h4>Tailored First Impression</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression. The immaculate fit does not reduce Bulk.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-reinforced-seam\"><h4>Steadfast Hem</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to Will saves against fear. Select the Mark condition when the incoming effect has the fear trait.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-hidden-pocketing\"><h4>Hidden Pocketing</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to conceal one appropriately sized carried object.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-quick-access-cut\"><h4>Quick-Access Cut</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Once per round, draw one stored light object as part of the action used to activate/use it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-universal-layered-lining\"><h4>Layered Lining</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Garment can accept one eligible secondary textile/leather component without increasing Bulk.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Universal · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Battlestitching</h2><p>Combat garments and armour liners designed for movement, access, protection, and adaptation.</p><h3>Signature — War Garments</h3><p>Create combat robes, coats, armour liners, harnesses and flexible protection.</p><h3>Mastery — Combat Cut</h3><p>Increase protection without sacrificing movement and reduce material waste when refitting worn gear.</p><h3>Legacy — Military Tailoring</h3><p>Supports elite uniforms, armour liners and specialised army equipment.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-combat-cut\"><h4>Combat Cut</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>Reduce one minor worn-equipment movement/fitting penalty and +1 Artisan bonus to Acrobatics checks involving the garment&#39;s mobility.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-quickdraw-harness\"><h4>Quickdraw Harness</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>Once per round, draw one secured light weapon/item as part of the action used to wield or activate it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-vital-reinforcement\"><h4>Vital Reinforcement</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>While attuned to worn armour/garment, gain Max HP equal to 5 × Core Tier. Does not stack with another Max-HP Artisan Mark.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-reactive-weave\"><h4>Reactive Weave</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Reaction once/round when damaged: reduce damage by Core Tier + 2; if attack was a critical hit, reduce by twice that amount.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-war-skin\"><h4>Duelist&#39;s War-Skin</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Worn armor grants a +1 untyped Artisan bonus to AC, a +10-foot untyped Artisan bonus to land Speed and a +2 untyped Artisan bonus to Reflex saves. It does not grant physical resistance.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-1-war-skin-regeneration\"><h4>War-Skin Regeneration</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>At start of each turn gain temp HP equal to 2 × Core Tier if you have none; if you took no damage since your previous turn, gain 3 × Core Tier instead.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Battlestitching · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Veilcraft</h2><p>Supernatural disguises, stealth clothing, concealing mantles, and perception-altering garments.</p><h3>Signature — Impossible Garments</h3><p>Manipulate sight, sound, shadow, identity and supernatural concealment through clothing.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Veil</h3><p>Improve disguise/concealment reliability and reduce the signs left by supernatural garments.</p><h3>Legacy — Shadow Service</h3><p>Supports scouts, spies, diplomats and intelligence networks.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-silent-stitch\"><h4>Silent Stitch</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to Stealth checks where clothing noise would matter.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-chameleon-cloth\"><h4>Chameleon Cloth</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Hide/Sneak while stationary or moving at half Speed in a chosen environment palette.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-many-faced-weave\"><h4>Many-Faced Weave</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>As a 1-minute adjustment, alter apparent clothing, silhouette and facial framing; gain +2 Artisan bonus to impersonation/disguise checks.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-shadow-mantle\"><h4>Shadow Mantle</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter for 1 minute gain concealment while in dim light or darkness; first successful Strike each round does not end it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-phase-veil\"><h4>Phase Veil</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/encounter for 1 round become partially incorporeal: move through creatures, gain physical resistance equal to 2 × Core Tier and ignore difficult terrain.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-2-null-mantle\"><h4>Null Mantle</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>Once/day for 1 minute become invisible to mundane sight and gain +2 Artisan bonus against magical detection/counteract attempts; attacking suppresses invisibility until start of next turn.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Veilcraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div><h2>Regaliacraft</h2><p>Vestments of authority supporting diplomacy, leadership, morale, royal courts, and prestige.</p><h3>Signature — Vestments of Authority</h3><p>Create royal, diplomatic, ceremonial and command garments that reinforce office and presence.</p><h3>Mastery — Perfect Regalia</h3><p>Regalia becomes stronger when properly tied to a recognised office, ruler or institution.</p><h3>Legacy — Royal Court</h3><p>Improves diplomacy, loyalty, leadership, festivals, prestige and foreign relations.</p><h3>Artisan Marks</h3><div class=\"cmt-guide-marks\"><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-court-finish\"><h4>Court Finish</h4><p><strong>minor · 0 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 1+ · item</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to Society checks involving formal protocol, heraldry or court presentation.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 1+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. Workshop consumables only.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-envoys-raiment\"><h4>Envoy&#39;s Raiment</h4><p><strong>standard · 1 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 2+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Diplomacy when acting in an official recognised capacity.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 2+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-commanders-mantle\"><h4>Commander&#39;s Mantle</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>Allies within 15 ft gain +1 Artisan bonus to Aid and saves against fear while wearer is conscious and visibly acting as leader.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-judicators-robes\"><h4>Judicator&#39;s Robes</h4><p><strong>major · 2 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 3+ · item</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to Sense Motive and checks to detect deliberate lies or enforce formal authority; once/encounter designate one creature as under judgement, granting +1 to allies&#39; first save against it.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 3+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 1 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-sovereign-presence\"><h4>Sovereign Presence</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>30-ft aura for 1 minute once/encounter: allies gain +1 Artisan bonus to saves and enemies take -1 Artisan penalty to fear/mental saves against the wearer.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article><article data-mark-id=\"tailoring-specialty-3-coronation-regalia\"><h4>Coronation Regalia</h4><p><strong>superior · 3 Capacity</strong> · Anchor Tier 4+ · item</p><p>While worn by the recognised office-holder, grant Max HP equal to 5 × Core Tier, +1 Artisan bonus to Diplomacy/Intimidation, and once/day give allies within 30 ft temp HP equal to 3 × Core Tier.</p><details><summary>Requirements & source</summary><p>Tailoring — Regaliacraft · Core Tier 4+</p><p>Anchors: lining, backing, wrap, cover, core. 2 material unit(s): herbs, leather, mana-crystals.</p></details></article></div></section>"}}]}
